against a 64-kDa antigen may be present in a patient with
a cerebella syndrome who was previously affected by
rigidity and spasms. Considering that the cerebellum is
filled with numerous GABAergic nerve terminals it is not
surprising that a patient harboring these Ab presents a
cerebella disorder. Our patient’s serum was not tested for
anti-GABAergic neuron Ah when rigidity and spasms
were present; however, ICA Ab were detected in that
period and it seems reasonable to assume that an autoim-
