logical symptoms.
On the other hand, the recent description of a paraneo-
plastic variant of stiff-man syndrome in which autoanti-
bodies other than anti-GABAergic neurons (with a clearly
different pattern of staining of the cerebellum recognizing
a 120-kDa antigen on Western blot) were detected (Folli et
al., 1993), shows that the same clinical picture could be an
expression of autoimmune damage to different CNS anti-
gens.
From the above remarks, it is clear that further studies
will be required before autoAb detection in biological
fluids and clinical symptoms can be currelakxl with diag-
